## Sodium acetate (trihydrate)
component-sodium-acetate = Sodium acetate (trihydrate)
    .genitive = sodium acetate
component-sodium-acetate-description-novice = White crystals — reusable hand warmers are made of them. Its solution can "forget" to crystallise, and then from a single crystal it suddenly sets and warms up.
component-sodium-acetate-description-school = A hot sodium acetate solution can be cooled below saturation and stay liquid — a supersaturated solution. Drop in a crystal (a seed), and the excess crystallises, giving off its heat of solution: the solution warms up.
component-sodium-acetate-safety-school = Irritates the eyes. The hot solution can burn.
component-sodium-acetate-model-notes = Crystallisation is instant: as soon as a supersaturated solution has a seed, it comes to equilibrium; the model does not compute crystals growing over time. Without a seed the solution does not crystallise by itself in the model.
